# Git hooks must keep LF endings.
#
# On Windows, `core.autocrlf` rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. For a shell
# script that corrupts the shebang — the interpreter path becomes `/bin/sh\r`,
# and the hook fails with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory". The hook
# then does not run, which is the one failure mode a secret-scanning hook must
# never have: it fails open, silently, on exactly the platform this repo is
# developed on.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
